<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Php on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/php/</link><description>Recent content in Php on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/php/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Patching php2shell in My Alpine Lighttpd PHP Docker Image</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/php2shell-alpine-lighttpd-php/</link><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/php2shell-alpine-lighttpd-php/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;If you use my &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php"&gt;alpine-lighttpd-php&lt;/a&gt; Docker image, please pull &lt;code&gt;:latest&lt;/code&gt; again and recreate your container. The image now runs &lt;strong&gt;PHP 8.4.27&lt;/strong&gt;, which fixes the php2shell vulnerabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="code-block"&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="code-copy" type="button" hidden aria-label="Copy code to clipboard"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="code-copy-label" aria-hidden="true"&gt;Copy&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;docker pull alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php:latest&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# or&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;docker pull ghcr.io/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php:latest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="what-is-php2shell"&gt;What is php2shell?&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;php2shell is the name for two PHP vulnerabilities, &lt;strong&gt;CVE-2026-109618&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;CVE-2026-109619&lt;/strong&gt;. Both are critical, and both allow remote code execution with no authentication. PHP published a &lt;a href="https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php#2026-10-21-5"&gt;security advisory&lt;/a&gt; on 21 October, alongside fixed releases 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36 and 8.2.35.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Lighttpd and PHP running on Docker Example</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lighttpd-and-php-running-on-docker/</link><pubDate>Mon, 18 Apr 2016 10:46:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lighttpd-and-php-running-on-docker/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 7 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Here is a low resource Lighttpd with PHP Docker image running on Alpine Linux, only ~37MB image.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Github = &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Docker Hub = &lt;a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php/"&gt;https://hub.docker.com/r/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Create an example PHP file in your local directory&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;echo "&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;?php phpinfo(); ?&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;" &amp;gt;&amp;gt; index.php&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Then start the Docker image;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;docker run --name "my-lighttpd-php" -p 8000:80 -v $(pwd):/var/www alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Browse to &lt;a href="http://localhost:8000/"&gt;http://localhost:8000/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgYWIck0V67HWxjgOpScXap5OEx2vv1gBjwCgyvR6BLSFY6UyA9KmMkeljWAO1qYnEBfaLGbzGRqyNlYZ0EIJ32tlzMwcGqmdowivbjtawBEZDlxGBQ27AgmsnDVKpHsp3A3Ej5fhdmykU/s1600/Screenshot%252B2016-04-18%252B10.44.29.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="227" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgYWIck0V67HWxjgOpScXap5OEx2vv1gBjwCgyvR6BLSFY6UyA9KmMkeljWAO1qYnEBfaLGbzGRqyNlYZ0EIJ32tlzMwcGqmdowivbjtawBEZDlxGBQ27AgmsnDVKpHsp3A3Ej5fhdmykU/s320/Screenshot%252B2016-04-18%252B10.44.29.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>